      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, sorry for not providing more context. See b/122738905\n\nBasically, in bionic tests, we have a makefile-defined module which uses an aptly named script \"touch-obj-on-success\"\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:bionic/tests/make_fortify_compile_test.mk;l\u003d5;drc\u003d9a2741010a93bfa08cc03e8d92c20c47d7e65abc\n\neffectively, the compile actions for these modules are expected to not produce output (due to COMPILATION_TESTS being defined), but are present to verify that the clang command succeeds.\n\nWe need a construct in Soong to migrate this to. See aosp/1370898 for the proposed usage.\n\nIIUC, NeverAllow is intended for interim use during migrations, whereas this might be a more permanent feature. WDYT?",
